  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Since&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>,</mo></math> so <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>We know that if two vectors&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;are perpendicular, then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Since,&nbsp;<math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> is perpendicular to <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> so</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>From equations&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> satisfies&nbsp;the above triplet.</p>",
